# For a vault kept as its own git repository (`wiki/.git`, e.g. for the
# Obsidian Git plugin). The skeleton ships without one; once there is one and
# ClaudeGitPushAll is enabled (it ships off), that sweep commits and pushes the
# vault every night. The pipeline's working files must never be part of that
# commit:
#
#   daily/.pending/   raw session tails dropped by the session-end and
#                     pre-compact hooks, waiting for a flush that has not run
#                     yet. They are UNPROCESSED transcript text — the input to
#                     the pipeline, not its output — so pushing them publishes
#                     verbatim session content (and, on a repo with a remote,
#                     publishes it off-box) hours before anything decided what
#                     belongs in the wiki at all.
#   .processed.json   the pipeline's state ledger, plus its lock and temp files.
#                     Machine-local bookkeeping: committing it means every clone
#                     of the vault claims to have already processed transcripts
#                     it has never seen, and two machines fight over the file on
#                     every pull.
#   last_success.json when each phase last succeeded on THIS machine (what
#                     bundle-status.py reports). Rewritten every night, and
#                     another machine's copy would report its runs as yours.
#
# The .gitkeep exception keeps the empty directory in the tree, which is what
# makes the skeleton deployable.
daily/.pending/*
!daily/.pending/.gitkeep
.processed.json
.processed.json.*
last_success.json
last_success.json.*
